{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyMAsNolK2cU8UW0L4ypyJI3"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#  Sequences with RNNs"],"metadata":{"id":"ckwxLsTpj5Co"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## What is a Sequence?\n","\n","A **sequence** is data where **order matters**.\n","\n","| Example | Why order matters |\n","|---------|-------------------|\n","| \"Dog bites man\" vs \"Man bites dog\" | Same words, completely different meaning |\n","| Stock prices: [100, 102, 98, 95] | Trend (going down) only visible in order |\n","| Video frames | Story makes sense only when frames are in sequence |\n","| Weather: [30°, 28°, 25°, 22°] | Temperature is dropping — order tells the pattern |\n","\n","### Why ANN fails with sequences:\n","\n","| Problem | Explanation |\n","|---------|-------------|\n","| Fixed input size | ANN needs fixed neurons — can't handle 3-word and 10-word sentences |\n","| No memory | Each input is processed independently, forgets previous inputs |\n","| Ignores order | \"I am happy\" and \"happy am I\" look the same to ANN |"],"metadata":{"id":"lPR40mG-kAOT"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## How RNN Works (Simple Explanation)\n","\n","RNN processes input **one step at a time** and passes a **hidden state** (memory) to the next step.\n","\n","```\n","Example: Processing \"I love NLP\"\n","\n","Step 1:  Input = \"I\"     →  Hidden state h1 = process(\"I\", empty)      → remembers: \"I\"\n","Step 2:  Input = \"love\"  →  Hidden state h2 = process(\"love\", h1)      → remembers: \"I love\"\n","Step 3:  Input = \"NLP\"   →  Hidden state h3 = process(\"NLP\", h2)       → remembers: \"I love NLP\"\n","                                                 ↓\n","                                          Final Output\n","```\n","\n","**Key idea:** At each step, RNN takes:\n","1. Current input (x_t)\n","2. Previous memory (h_t-1)\n","\n","And produces:\n","1. New memory (h_t)\n","2. Output (optional — depends on the type!)\n","\n","**Formula:** `h_t = tanh(W_xh * x_t + W_hh * h_(t-1) + b)`\n","\n","The **same weights** are used at every step — this is called **weight sharing**. This is why RNN can handle any length input."],"metadata":{"id":"02aRjLi8kHI9"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["---\n","\n","## 4 Types of RNN Architectures\n","\n","The key question: **Where do we take the output?**\n","\n","```\n","1. One-to-One        2. One-to-Many        3. Many-to-One       4. Many-to-Many\n","\n","   [y]                 [y1][y2][y3]            [y]               [y1][y2][y3]\n","    |                    |   |   |              |                  |   |   |\n","   [h]                 [h]→[h]→[h]           [h]→[h]→[h]        [h]→[h]→[h]\n","    |                    |                    |   |   |           |   |   |\n","   [x]                 [x]                  [x1][x2][x3]       [x1][x2][x3]\n","\n","  1 in → 1 out       1 in → many out      many in → 1 out    many in → many out\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"QwcD8sqBkM4W"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import matplotlib.patches as mpatches\n","\n","def draw_rnn_type(ax, title, inputs, hiddens, outputs, connections):\n","    ax.set_xlim(-0.5, max(len(inputs), len(outputs))-0.5)\n","    ax.set_ylim(-0.5, 3.5)\n","    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n","    ax.axis('off')\n","\n","    # Draw nodes\n","    for i, x in enumerate(inputs):\n","        ax.add_patch(plt.Circle((x, 0), 0.25, color='#4CAF50', zorder=5))\n","        ax.text(x, 0, f'x{i+1}', ha='center', va='center', fontsize=9, color='white', fontweight='bold')\n","    for i, h in enumerate(hiddens):\n","        ax.add_patch(plt.Circle((h, 1.5), 0.25, color='#2196F3', zorder=5))\n","        ax.text(h, 1.5, f'h{i+\n","        1}', ha='center', va='center', fontsize=9, color='white', fontweight='bold')\n","    for i, y in enumerate(outputs):\n","        ax.add_patch(plt.Circle((y, 3), 0.25, color='#F44336', zorder=5))\n","        ax.text(y, 3, f'y{i+1}', ha='center', va='center', fontsize=9, color='white', fontweight='bold')\n","\n","    # Draw connections\n","    for (x1, y1, x2, y2) in connections:\n","        ax.annotate('', xy=(x2, y2-0.25), xytext=(x1, y1+0.25),\n","                   arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='->', color='gray', lw=1.5))\n","\n","    # Hidden-to-hidden arrows\n","    for i in range(len(hiddens)-1):\n","        ax.annotate('', xy=(hiddens[i+1]-0.25, 1.5), xytext=(hiddens[i]+0.25, 1.5),\n","                   arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='->', color='#FF9800', lw=2))\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 4, figsize=(16, 4))\n","\n","# One-to-One\n","draw_rnn_type(axes[0], \"One-to-One\", [0], [0], [0],\n","              [(0,0,0,1.5), (0,1.5,0,3)])\n","\n","# One-to-Many\n","draw_rnn_type(axes[1], \"One-to-Many\", [0], [0,1,2], [0,1,2],\n","              [(0,0,0,1.5), (0,1.5,0,3), (1,1.5,1,3), (2,1.5,2,3)])\n","\n","# Many-to-One\n","draw_rnn_type(axes[2], \"Many-to-One\", [0,1,2], [0,1,2], [2],\n","              [(0,0,0,1.5), (1,0,1,1.5), (2,0,2,1.5), (2,1.5,2,3)])\n","\n","# Many-to-Many\n","draw_rnn_type(axes[3], \"Many-to-Many\", [0,1,2], [0,1,2], [0,1,2],\n","              [(0,0,0,1.5), (1,0,1,1.5), (2,0,2,1.5), (0,1.5,0,3), (1,1.5,1,3), (2,1.5,2,3)])\n","\n","# Legend\n","fig.legend([mpatches.Patch(color='#4CAF50'), mpatches.Patch(color='#2196F3'),\n","            mpatches.Patch(color='#F44336'), mpatches.Patch(color='#FF9800')],\n","           ['Input', 'Hidden State', 'Output', 'Time Flow →'],\n","           loc='lower center', ncol=4, fontsize=11)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.subplots_adjust(bottom=0.15)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":275},"id":"i8TCkfzD1VRI","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787035152471,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":5477,"user":{"displayName":"Datamites 20","userId":"1431